===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|now|_|literary}} Someone who drinks a lot; a [[drunkard]].
#: {{syn|en|alcoholic|drunkard|tosspot|Thesaurus:drunkard}}
#* '''1818''', {{w|John Keats}},  “On Some Skulls in Beauly Abbey, near Inverness”:
#*: A '''Toper''' this! He plied his glass<br>More strictly than he said the Mass,  […]
#* '''1851''', Herman Melville, ''Moby-Dick'':
#*: The liquor soon mounted into their heads, as it generally does even with the arrantest '''topers''' newly landed from sea, and they began capering about most obstreperously.
#* '''1863''', Sheridan Le Fanu, ''{{w|The House by the Churchyard}}''
#*: Mrs. Irons rebelled in her bed, and refused peremptorily to get up again, to furnish the musical '''topers''' with rum and lemons {{...}}

